.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/esquery Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
ESQuery is a library for querying the AST output by Esprima for patterns of syntax using a CSS style selector system\&. Check out the demo:

.PP
\fRdemo\fP

.PP
The following selectors are supported:
.IP "\(bu" 2
AST node type: \fRForStatement\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRwildcard\fP: \fR*\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRattribute existence\fP: \fR[attr]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRattribute value\fP: \fR[attr="foo"]\fP or \fR[attr=123]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
attribute regex: \fR[attr=/foo\&.*/]\fP or (with flags) \fR[attr=/foo\&.*/is]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
attribute conditions: \fR[attr!="foo"]\fP, \fR[attr>2]\fP, \fR[attr<3]\fP, \fR[attr>=2]\fP, or \fR[attr<=3]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
nested attribute: \fR[attr\&.level2="foo"]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
field: \fRFunctionDeclaration > Identifier\&.id\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRFirst\fP or \fRlast\fP child: \fR:first-child\fP or \fR:last-child\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnth-child\fP (no ax+b support): \fR:nth-child(2)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnth-last-child\fP (no ax+b support): \fR:nth-last-child(1)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdescendant\fP: \fRancestor descendant\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRchild\fP: \fRparent > child\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfollowing sibling\fP: \fRnode ~ sibling\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRadjacent sibling\fP: \fRnode + adjacent\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnegation\fP: \fR:not(ForStatement)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRhas\fP: \fR:has(ForStatement)\fP, \fR:has(> ForStatement)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRmatches-any\fP: \fR:matches([attr] > :first-child, :last-child)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsubject indicator\fP: \fR!IfStatement > [name="foo"]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
class of AST node: \fR:statement\fP, \fR:expression\fP, \fR:declaration\fP, \fR:function\fP, or \fR:pattern\fP
.PP

.PP
\fR\fP 
